  Quote of the Week:

  Desierius Erasmus, Dutch scholar, 1521:
  "Let a King recall that to improve his realm is better than to increase 
his territory."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  Agesilao treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Agesilao treated with his ally Prometeo 
(#5).  Agesilao treated with his ally II Kahn (#6).  Agesilao treated with 
his ally Giovanna (#7).
  With the advent of the spring season, Agesilao set out to quench his 
thirst for glory.  He cast a Plague spell.  Bizerte was hit by a plague.  
The plague struck the 125th Phalanx in Bizerte and destroyed them.  The 
plague struck the 134th Warg Riders in Bizerte and destroyed them.  The 
plague struck the 136th Warg Riders in Bizerte and destroyed them.  His 
experience raised his aptitude in Necromancy.
  Black Forest was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Black 
Forest.
  In early summer, Agesilao journeyed to Mare Frigidis.
  With the advent of the late summer season, Agesilao unsheathed his weapon 
and entered the Catacombs warily.  Agesilao wielded his Holy Sword.  He 
encountered the Troll.  Uttering his syllables of magic with trained 
precision, Agesilao let fly a Hand Of Death spell and began making squeezing 
motions with his hands.
  The Troll loped along smoothly and closed to bow range.  Agesilao clenched 
his fist, squeezing the intestines of the Troll and scored on the Troll, 
doing 3 points of damage.
  The Troll closed to melee range, seething with maniacal blood-lust.  
The Troll whirled about and smashed at Agesilao but Agesilao dodged the 
blow.  The unseen hands of Agesilao grasped its lungs, squeezing the Troll 
and walloped the Troll with 3 damage points.  The Troll smashed at Agesilao 
but its club whiffed harmlessly through the air.  Agesilao's invisible 
fingers pierced the eyes of the Troll and clawed at its brain and scored 3 
damage points on the Troll.
  The Troll angrily assailed Agesilao but its aim was slightly off the mark. 
Agesilao grabbed its spine with unseen hands and shook it ruthlessly and 
damaged the Troll, scoring 3 damage points.  The Troll turned away Agesilao 
with its aggressive assault.  The Troll then swang at Agesilao with maximum 
force and would have hit Agesilao if Agesilao hadn't sidestepped.  Agesilao 
brought his hands together and pulled them apart in a tearing gesture, 
provoking a blood-curdling squeal of pain from the Troll and inflicted 3 
damage points.  The Troll swang at Agesilao and missed badly.  Agesilao 
wrapped his phantasmal hand around the Troll's heart and squeezed it 
viciously and scored on the Troll, doing 3 points of damage.
  The Troll skillfully smashed at Agesilao but Agesilao dodged the club.  
Agesilao clenched his fist, squeezing the innards of the Troll and walloped 
the Troll with 3 damage points.  The Troll smashed at Agesilao but its club 
whiffed through the air.  The invisible hands of Agesilao grabbed its lungs, 
choking the life out of the Troll and inflicted 3 damage points on the Troll.
  The Troll feigned panic, then whirled and smashed at Agesilao but its aim 
was slightly off.  Agesilao's invisible fingers pierced the forehead of 
the Troll and clawed at its brain and damaged the Troll, scoring 3 damage 
points.  The Troll flamboyantly vaulted over Agesilao and deftly swang at 
him and would have struck him if Agesilao hadn't ducked.  Agesilao grabbed 
its spine with phantasmal hands and shook it and inflicted 3 damage points.  
The Troll fell, fatally injured.  Agesilao sacked the treasure of the Troll. 
Agesilao bagged the Large Hoard of Gold.  Agesilao located a treasure of 19 
gold and snarfed it up.  Agesilao hailed the Roulette Wheel.
  Magic runes formed on the Roulette Wheel, saying "The effects of the 
Roulette Wheel are both good and bad!  Chance will determine the fate of 
Agesilao, good or ill.  Care to take a chance?  I give you the power to cast 
a Earthquake spell!"  Agesilao invoked the power of the Roulette Wheel in 
the Catacombs, from which Mare Frigidis was devastated by an earthquake!
  During fall, Agesilao rode into Mare Ritalis.
  The Sahuagin Sea was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in 
the Sahuagin Sea.
  With the advent of the early winter season, Agesilao took a deep, nervous 
gulp from his bottle of vodka, and entered the Pyramid.  Agesilao drew out 
his Holy Sword.  He encountered the Basilisk.  Incanting a Hand Of Death 
spell, Agesilao directed scintillating, writhing strands of magic and began 
making squeezing motions with his hands.
  The Basilisk loped along steadily, conserving its energy, and closed to 
bow range.  Agesilao curled his phantasmal hand around the Basilisk's liver 
and squeezed it and walloped the Basilisk with 3 damage points.
  The Basilisk rushed into melee combat.  The Basilisk lunged at Agesilao 
but its aim was just off the mark.  Agesilao clenched his fist tightly, 
squeezing the innards of the Basilisk and scored 3 damage points on 
the Basilisk.
  The Basilisk deftly snapped at Agesilao and would have struck him if 
Agesilao hadn't ducked just then.  The invisible hands of Agesilao grasped 
its throat, squeezing the breath out of the Basilisk and damaged 
the Basilisk, inflicting 3 damage points.  The Basilisk lunged at Agesilao 
with all its might and missed badly.  Agesilao's invisible fingers pierced 
the eyes of the Basilisk and dug into its brain and inflicted 3 damage 
points.  The Basilisk whirled around and snapped at Agesilao but Agesilao 
dodged the blow.  Agesilao grabbed its neck with phantasmal hands and shook 
it and scored on the Basilisk, doing 3 points of damage.
  The Basilisk feigned retreat, then pivoted and lunged at Agesilao but its 
jaws whiffed through the air.  Agesilao brought his hands together and 
yanked them apart in a ripping motion, provoking a terrible squeal of pain 
from the Basilisk and scorched the Basilisk with 3 damage points.  
The Basilisk then snapped at Agesilao but its aim was just off.  Agesilao 
wrapped his phantasmal hand around the Basilisk's liver and squeezed it 
viciously and scored 3 damage points on the Basilisk.  The Basilisk 
staggered, stunned by the force of the mortal blow.  Agesilao turned his 
attention to the hoard of the Basilisk.  Agesilao walked over to a pile of 
treasure and secured the Large Hoard of Gold.  Agesilao took 14 gold from 
the treasure trove of the Basilisk.
  Agesilao saw nothing special while scouting out the Pyramid.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Agesilao for this year.


  Agesilao treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Agesilao treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).
Agesilao treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally II Kahn (#6).  Agesilao treated with his ally Giovanna (#7).  Agesilao 
treated with his ally Circe (#8).

  Here is the financial report for Agesilao's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 19 gold in revenue.  2 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  2 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Agesilao was left 
with 140 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Negumba
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I journeyed to Black Forest.
  With the coming of the early summer season I could find no soldiers in 
Black Forest for the requested Garrison troops.  Instead, I tried hard to 
improve my Element Magic, but I practiced in vain.
  With the advent of the late summer season, I moved into the First Sea.
  The hot days of summer surrendered to fall.  I could find no soldiers in 
the First Sea for the requested Garrison troops.  Instead, I discovered 
nothing in my sagely researches.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I explored the First Sea 
thoroughly, leaving no stone unturned, and our exploration level there has 
risen to 97%.
  Speaking with friendly adventurers, I learned a rumor about a previously 
unheard of Tower in Abu Matariq (#106), held by the Witch, who according to 
legend possesses the Huge Hoard of Gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Negumba


